<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via four-day fixed system RPs.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via four-day fixed system RPs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added temporary reserves to the banking system through four-day fixed system repurchase agreements, a Fed spokeswoman confirmed.</p>
<p>Analysts had anticipated a small system repurchase operation, citing low Treasury balances at the Fed.</p>
<p>Federal funds were trading at a relatively soft 5-7/16 percent, below the Fed's 5-1/2 percent target for the rate, at the time of the operation.</p>
<p>(( -- North American Treasury Desk 212-859-1679))</p>
